menu "MAO power"

    config MAO_POWER_WAKE_INTERVAL_MIN
        int "Deep-sleep housekeeping wake-up interval (minutes)"
        range 1 1440
        default 30
        help
            Timer wake-up while in deep sleep, so MAO can update its state
            (battery, time asleep) even when nobody touches it.

    config MAO_POWER_CRITICAL_SHUTDOWN
        bool "Deep sleep on a critical battery"
        default y
        help
            On battery with SOC <= 2 % or the cell below 3.35 V (three
            readings in a row), post MAO_EVENT_BATTERY_CRITICAL, give the
            application 5 s to save state, then deep-sleep with USB as the
            only wake source. The hardware UVLO switches the 3V3 rail off
            near 2.96 V VSYS; this keeps the firmware well clear of it.

    config MAO_POWER_AUTO
        bool "Automatic power states (ACTIVE / IDLE / DROWSY / DEEP SLEEP)"
        default y
        help
            Let MAO doze off on its own: IDLE after a short while without
            anyone around (sensors slower), DROWSY later (panel asleep, CPU
            light-sleeping between wake events), DEEP SLEEP after a long
            doze on battery. Boards without power management ignore this.
            Without it, only "mao sleep" and a critical battery change the
            power state.

    config MAO_POWER_IDLE_AFTER_S
        int "IDLE after this many seconds without activity"
        depends on MAO_POWER_AUTO
        range 5 3600
        default 30

    config MAO_POWER_DROWSY_AFTER_S
        int "DROWSY after this many seconds without activity"
        depends on MAO_POWER_AUTO
        range 20 86400
        default 180
        help
            The application's sleepy look (MAO_SLEEPY_TIMEOUT_S, dimmed
            screen, heavy eyes) comes first; DROWSY then puts the panel to
            sleep and light-sleeps the CPU.

    config MAO_POWER_DEEP_AFTER_MIN
        int "DEEP SLEEP after this many minutes DROWSY (0 = never)"
        depends on MAO_POWER_AUTO
        range 0 1440
        default 30

    config MAO_POWER_REDROWSE_S
        int "After a wake nobody follows up, doze off again after (s)"
        depends on MAO_POWER_AUTO
        range 5 600
        default 20
        help
            A bump of the desk or a passing shadow wakes MAO from DROWSY;
            if nothing else happens it looks around this long, then dozes
            off again instead of waiting the full DROWSY delay.

    config MAO_POWER_SLEEP_WITH_CONSOLE
        bool "Sleep even while a USB host uses the console"
        depends on MAO_POWER_AUTO
        default n
        help
            Light and deep sleep drop the USB-Serial/JTAG connection. By
            default MAO never goes below IDLE while a USB host is attached
            (start-of-frame packets seen), so development sessions and the
            factory fixture keep their console.

    config MAO_POWER_DEEP_ON_USB
        bool "Deep sleep while on USB power"
        depends on MAO_POWER_AUTO
        default n
        help
            On a charger MAO dozes (DROWSY) but stays out of deep sleep by
            default, so it wakes instantly and keeps its sense of time.

    config MAO_POWER_QUIET_WAKE_S
        int "Look-around time after a housekeeping timer wake (s)"
        depends on MAO_POWER_AUTO
        range 2 120
        default 8
        help
            The deep-sleep housekeeping timer boots MAO with the screen
            dark. If nothing happens within this time it goes straight
            back to deep sleep.

endmenu
